The two nebula trails are more limited: nebula-data-events-trail only covers S3 data events for one bucket in us-east-1 (no management events), and nebula-single-region-trail only has default management event coverage in us-east-1 with no global service events; both have log file validation disabled. There are real coverage gaps—other buckets' data events, other regions, no org-wide aggregation visible, and no integrity digest despite CloudTrail's "immutable" claims—plus Event History caps out at 90 days and excludes data events, so I should flag all this clearly in the answer.

